    <h2 class="page-title">Bio</h2>

    <div class="article-content">
        <p>
            Hi, I'm Antoine. I write here about physics, technology, economics, and the ideas where they meet.
        </p>
        <p>
            This blog is a place to think out loud: long-form notes, half-formed questions, and the occasional deep dive when something won't leave me alone.
        </p>
        <p>
            I'm also a father of two boys. A lot of my energy outside work goes into teaching them the fundamentals, how to think critically, and how to navigate a world where AI is woven into almost everything — without letting the tools do the thinking for them.
        </p>
        <p>
            When I'm not writing, I'm usually reading, building things, or trying to understand how something works well enough to explain it simply — often to an audience of one or two at the kitchen table.
        </p>

        <h3>Work</h3>
        <p>
            Professionally, I've spent years in <strong>software</strong>, <strong>security</strong>, and <strong>AI</strong> — often where sales, product, and engineering meet. I've been a solutions engineer and field architect, led engineering teams, and more recently focused on <strong>forward deployed</strong> and field engineering: getting close to customers, translating between technical and business context, and helping teams ship something that actually works.
        </p>
        <p>
            Currently part of the amazing <a href="https://www.tenzai.com/"><strong>Tenzai</strong></a> team, building autonomous and pairable AI hackers to even the playing field — so businesses can stay resilient in the face of AI-powered hacking.
        </p>
